Train Opt Skills contains original project code, skill instructions, and a
user-provided training optimization guide. The MIT license covers original
project material; it does not relicense external linked articles, documentation,
models, datasets, or trademarks.

Project organization was informed by anthropics/skills, obra/superpowers,
vercel-labs/agent-skills, K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills, and the Agent Skills
specification. No source implementations from those projects are bundled.
See docs/design-references.md for links and details.

The supplied Chinese guide is preserved in docs/
training_performance_optimization_guide_zh_v2.md with its own source list.
Its original case-study source is https://juejin.cn/post/7676104122035847231 .
The supplemental user text is described by the guide but is not redistributed
as a raw attachment. Reported case-study gains are not project benchmarks.
This project has no affiliation with the referenced organizations.


Domain workflow references additionally include NVIDIA/skills, meta-pytorch/skills,
AMD-AGI/Primus and NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM. Integration metadata links to a reviewed
Meta PyTorch commit; no third-party skill source is redistributed.
